# Q everywhere: IC16's input 3B (CHAR_FETCH) is stuck high, so the load gate no longer waits for a character fetch: every memory access loads a glyph. The HALT ($76) that ends each row loads the one of code $36, Q, and the halted processor's fetches of the byte after it repeat that byte's glyph to the row's end: mostly the next row's HALT, Q again, or the next row's first character. The margins, where the ROM's own code runs, fill up with its codes' glyphs as well.
machine bw80
title "Q everywhere"
brief "The BW-80 works, but the empty places on the screen fill up with letters, Qs mostly, and the margins around the picture are full of junk. What is typed shows over them."
fault stuck IC16.3B 1
